When you have a  web application(single page applications e.g react,regular not html etc),there are 2 layers of it
a)ui layer (ui layer is everything that you see on the browser e.g btns,colors,headings etc)
b)Data layer

Both combined to make a react application

How to show data on browser in react aplication?
We can show that on browser by state & props.

What is diff btw state and prop?
Suppose if you have a container and you want a variable which has a scope just with in a container,it is known as state
 while prop is the value passed from one component to another component
 
 Imp:
 Props are kind of local state of our parent component
 
 
 Props Drillings:
 
 Props drilling is when you pass data from a parent component to a deeply nested child component through multiple layers of components — even if the middle components don’t use that data.
 
 Example:
 function App() {
  const username = "Alice";
  return <Parent username={username} />;
}

function Parent({ username }) {
  return <Child username={username} />;
}

function Child({ username }) {
  return <GrandChild username={username} />;
}

function GrandChild({ username }) {
  return <p>Hello, {username}!</p>;
}

Problems:
Becomes messy as your app grows
Harder to maintain or refactor
Components get bloated with unused props

